{"toolCallId":"edit:0#586f844c7dfd4459b0f16426477d1d85","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/217-weak-model-spec-authoring/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add a QUIET_OUTPUT flag and one output branch to recommend-level.sh so --quiet prints only the recommended-level line; verified by a line count and an empty diff of default output.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash (bash 3.2-compatible, `set -euo pipefail`) |\n| **Framework** | None — single CLI script |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | Manual shell verification (`bash -n`, `diff`, `wc -l`, `rg`); regression via `tests/test-phase-system.js` and `tests/test-phase-validation.js` |\n\n### Overview\nThe change adds one `QUIET_OUTPUT` global, one `--quiet|-q` case to the option parser, and one early branch in the output dispatch that prints `Recommended Level: N (Name)` before the text/JSON selection. Scoring, level determination, and every existing output path run unchanged, which keeps the default report byte-identical.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented in `spec.md` §2–§3\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable — SC-001 through SC-003 are command-checkable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified — bash only; test consumers named in §6\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met — every `acceptance-criteria.md` row is `Met`\n- [ ] Tests passing — `node tests/test-phase-system.js` and `node tests/test-phase-validation.js` exit 0\n- [ ] Docs updated — spec/plan/tasks agree on the flag, its alias, and the quiet-wins rule\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-script output branch (Other)\n\n### Key Components\n- **Option parser** (`recommend-level.sh` argument loop): accepts `--quiet`/`-q` and sets `QUIET_OUTPUT=true`\n- **Output dispatch** (`recommend-level.sh` section 7): quiet branch prints the level line before the JSON/text selection\n\n### Data Flow\nCommand-line args → globals (`QUIET_OUTPUT`) → scoring functions → `determine_level` → output dispatch: quiet prints one line, otherwise the existing text/JSON report runs.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\nThis is a feature addition rather than a fix, but the change touches stdout format, so the producer/consumer inventory is kept.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` | producer — owns stdout format | update | `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch |\n| `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` | consumer — parses `--json` stdout strictly | unchanged | `node tests/test-phase-system.js` exits 0 |\n| `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js` | consumer — parses `--json` output | unchanged | `node tests/test-phase-validation.js` exits 0 |\n| `runtime/cli/spec/README.md` | docs — one-line script description | unchanged — the one-liner stays accurate | `rg -n 'recommend-level' spec/README.md` |\n| `references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md` | docs — shows non-quiet usage | not a consumer — could adopt `--quiet` later | `rg -n 'recommend-level' references/workflows/` |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` — one producer line inside `output_text`; the quiet branch reuses it.\n- Consumers of changed output: `rg -ln 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/` — the two test files above, both `--json`-only callers.\n- Matrix axes: mode {text, json} × quiet {absent, present} = 4 rows, plus the `-q` alias row; all five are verified in `tasks.md` Phase 3.\n- Algorithm invariant: scoring and phase logic run identically in every mode; only the output dispatch reads `QUIET_OUTPUT`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state. Setup captures the baseline output, Implementation adds the flag and its docs, Verification diffs and counts lines.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Syntax | `recommend-level.sh` parses | `bash -n` |\n| Manual | Quiet contract: one line, alias, `--json` precedence, error paths | `bash`, `wc -l`, `rg`, `diff` against `scratch/` baselines |\n| Regression | Existing `--json` consumers | `node tests/test-phase-system.js`, `node tests/test-phase-validation.js` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| bash (3.2+) | External | Green | Already required; the flag uses only existing constructs |\n| `tests/test-phase-system.js` | Internal | Green | Loses the strictest JSON regression check |\n| `tests/test-phase-validation.js` | Internal | Green | Loses the phase-fields JSON regression check |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: default output differs from baseline, or the quiet line is missing/malformed\n- **Procedure**: revert the single-file edit to `recommend-level.sh`, then rerun the two baseline diffs to confirm the restore\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core |\n| Core | Setup | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 20 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 15 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **~45 minutes (assumption)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Baseline text and JSON captures exist under `scratch/` (no data to back up)\n- [ ] Feature flag: N/A — the flag itself is the toggle\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts: N/A — CLI script, no service\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Restore `recommend-level.sh` to its pre-change content (revert the file)\n2. Rerun `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15` and diff against the baseline capture\n3. Rerun `node tests/test-phase-system.js` to confirm JSON consumers recover\n4. Notify stakeholders: N/A — internal tooling script\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌──────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐\n│  Baseline capture │────►│  Flag + dispatch  │────►│  Diff + verify   │\n│  (scratch/)       │     │  (recommend-level)│     │  (wc/diff/node)  │\n└──────────────────┘     └──────────────────┘     └──────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture | None | `scratch/baseline-{text,json}.txt` | Diff verification |\n| Flag + dispatch edit | Baseline capture | `QUIET_OUTPUT`, `--quiet|-q`, quiet branch | Diff + verify |\n| Help/header docs | None | `--quiet` documentation | Close |\n| Diff + verify | Flag edit, baselines, docs | Empty diffs, one-line output, passing tests | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Setup: baseline capture** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Core: flag, dispatch branch, docs** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Verify: diffs, quiet checks, test scripts, validate.sh** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: ~45 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- Help text and header comment edits can proceed alongside the dispatch branch (same file, separate regions)\n- Baseline capture can run while the edit is being drafted\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | `scratch/baseline-text.txt` and `scratch/baseline-json.txt` exist; text file holds 16 lines | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Flag implemented | `bash -n` exits 0; `--quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)` on one line | Phase 2 |\n| M3 | Verified | Both diffs empty, test scripts exit 0, `validate.sh --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED` | Phase 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Quiet prints the existing `Recommended Level: N (Name)` line\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: `--quiet` must print the recommended level in a form callers can parse. The text report already emits exactly that line.\n\n**Decision**: The quiet branch echoes `Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})`, the identical label `output_text` uses.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- One label serves humans and machines; REQ-001's regex pins it\n- A label change would now break quiet callers too — mitigated by the pinned regex\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Bare digit (`2`): loses the level name and diverges from the label a caller may already match\n- `level=2` key=value form: invents a second contract where one already exists\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: `--quiet` takes precedence over `--json`\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: `--quiet --json` is ambiguous — quiet promises one line, JSON promises a parseable document.\n\n**Decision**: When `QUIET_OUTPUT` is true, the script prints the single text line regardless of `JSON_OUTPUT`.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Quiet's contract stays absolute: exactly one line, always\n- A JSON-expecting caller that adds `--quiet` gets non-JSON — mitigated by documenting the rule in help; no current caller passes both flags\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Minimal JSON `{\"recommended_level\": N}`: a third output format for no current caller; the strict JSON tests parse the full document anyway\n- Rejecting the combination with an error: breaks normal flag composability for no safety gain\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add a QUIET_OUTPUT flag and one output branch to recommend-level.sh so --quiet prints only the recommended-level line; verified by a line count and an empty diff of default output.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash (bash 3.2-compatible, `set -euo pipefail`) |\n| **Framework** | None — single CLI script |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | Manual shell verification (`bash -n`, `diff`, `wc -l`, `rg`); regression via `tests/test-phase-system.js` and `tests/test-phase-validation.js` |\n\n### Overview\nThe change adds one `QUIET_OUTPUT` global, one `--quiet|-q` case to the option parser, and one early branch in the output dispatch that prints `Recommended Level: N (Name)` before the text/JSON selection. Scoring, level determination, and every existing output path run unchanged, which keeps the default report byte-identical.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented in `spec.md` §2–§3\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable — SC-001 through SC-003 are command-checkable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified — bash only; test consumers named in §6\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met — every `acceptance-criteria.md` row is `Met`\n- [ ] Tests passing — `node tests/test-phase-system.js` and `node tests/test-phase-validation.js` exit 0\n- [ ] Docs updated — spec/plan/tasks agree on the flag, its alias, and the quiet-wins rule\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-script output branch (Other)\n\n### Key Components\n- **Option parser** (`recommend-level.sh` argument loop): accepts `--quiet`/`-q` and sets `QUIET_OUTPUT=true`\n- **Output dispatch** (`recommend-level.sh` section 7): quiet branch prints the level line before the JSON/text selection\n\n### Data Flow\nCommand-line args → globals (`QUIET_OUTPUT`) → scoring functions → `determine_level` → output dispatch: quiet prints one line, otherwise the existing text/JSON report runs.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\nThis is a feature addition rather than a fix, but the change touches stdout format, so the producer/consumer inventory is kept.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` | producer — owns stdout format | update | `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch |\n| `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` | consumer — parses `--json` stdout strictly | unchanged | `node tests/test-phase-system.js` exits 0 |\n| `runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js` | consumer — parses `--json` output | unchanged | `node tests/test-phase-validation.js` exits 0 |\n| `runtime/cli/spec/README.md` | docs — one-line script description | unchanged — the one-liner stays accurate | `rg -n 'recommend-level' spec/README.md` |\n| `references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md` | docs — shows non-quiet usage | not a consumer — could adopt `--quiet` later | `rg -n 'recommend-level' references/workflows/` |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` — one producer line inside `output_text`; the quiet branch reuses it.\n- Consumers of changed output: `rg -ln 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/` — the two test files above, both `--json`-only callers.\n- Matrix axes: mode {text, json} × quiet {absent, present} = 4 rows, plus the `-q` alias row; all five are verified in `tasks.md` Phase 3.\n- Algorithm invariant: scoring and phase logic run identically in every mode; only the output dispatch reads `QUIET_OUTPUT`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state. Setup captures the baseline output, Implementation adds the flag and its docs, Verification diffs and counts lines.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Syntax | `recommend-level.sh` parses | `bash -n` |\n| Manual | Quiet contract: one line, alias, `--json` precedence, error paths | `bash`, `wc -l`, `rg`, `diff` against `scratch/` baselines |\n| Regression | Existing `--json` consumers | `node tests/test-phase-system.js`, `node tests/test-phase-validation.js` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| bash (3.2+) | External | Green | Already required; the flag uses only existing constructs |\n| `tests/test-phase-system.js` | Internal | Green | Loses the strictest JSON regression check |\n| `tests/test-phase-validation.js` | Internal | Green | Loses the phase-fields JSON regression check |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: default output differs from baseline, or the quiet line is missing/malformed\n- **Procedure**: revert the single-file edit to `recommend-level.sh`, then rerun the two baseline diffs to confirm the restore\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core |\n| Core | Setup | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 20 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 15 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **~45 minutes (assumption)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Baseline text and JSON captures exist under `scratch/` (no data to back up)\n- [ ] Feature flag: N/A — the flag itself is the toggle\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts: N/A — CLI script, no service\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Restore `recommend-level.sh` to its pre-change content (revert the file)\n2. Rerun `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15` and diff against the baseline capture\n3. Rerun `node tests/test-phase-system.js` to confirm JSON consumers recover\n4. Notify stakeholders: N/A — internal tooling script\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌──────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐\n│  Baseline capture │────►│  Flag + dispatch  │────►│  Diff + verify   │\n│  (scratch/)       │     │  (recommend-level)│     │  (wc/diff/node)  │\n└──────────────────┘     └──────────────────┘     └──────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture | None | `scratch/baseline-{text,json}.txt` | Diff verification |\n| Flag + dispatch edit | Baseline capture | `QUIET_OUTPUT`, `--quiet|-q`, quiet branch | Diff + verify |\n| Help/header docs | None | `--quiet` documentation | Close |\n| Diff + verify | Flag edit, baselines, docs | Empty diffs, one-line output, passing tests | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Setup: baseline capture** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Core: flag, dispatch branch, docs** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Verify: diffs, quiet checks, test scripts, validate.sh** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: ~45 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- Help text and header comment edits can proceed alongside the dispatch branch (same file, separate regions)\n- Baseline capture can run while the edit is being drafted\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | `scratch/baseline-text.txt` and `scratch/baseline-json.txt` exist; text file holds 16 lines | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Flag implemented | `bash -n` exits 0; `--quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)` on one line | Phase 2 |\n| M3 | Verified | Both diffs empty, test scripts exit 0, `validate.sh --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED` | Phase 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Quiet prints the existing `Recommended Level: N (Name)` line\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: `--quiet` must print the recommended level in a form callers can parse. The text report already emits exactly that line.\n\n**Decision**: The quiet branch echoes `Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})`, the identical label `output_text` uses.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- One label serves humans and machines; REQ-001's regex pins it\n- A label change would now break quiet callers too — mitigated by the pinned regex\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Bare digit (`2`): loses the level name and diverges from the label a caller may already match\n- `level=2` key=value form: invents a second contract where one already exists\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: `--quiet` takes precedence over `--json`\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: `--quiet --json` is ambiguous — quiet promises one line, JSON promises a parseable document.\n\n**Decision**: When `QUIET_OUTPUT` is true, the script prints the single text line regardless of `JSON_OUTPUT`.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- Quiet's contract stays absolute: exactly one line, always\n- A JSON-expecting caller that adds `--quiet` gets non-JSON — mitigated by documenting the rule in help; no current caller passes both flags\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Minimal JSON `{\"recommended_level\": N}`: a third output format for no current caller; the strict JSON tests parse the full document anyway\n- Rejecting the combination with an error: breaks normal flag composability for no safety gain\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ai-execution -->\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n- [ ] Read spec.md, this plan, and tasks.md before the first edit\n- [ ] Confirm the only code target is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`\n- [ ] Know the task's `Verify:` command before starting it\n- [ ] Baseline captures exist under `scratch/` before any Phase 2 edit (T002)\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Requirement |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Execute tasks in order; T005 and T006 may run parallel to T004 inside the same edit session |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Touch only `recommend-level.sh` and this packet's files; report anything else as a finding |\n| TASK-VERIFY | Run the task's `Verify:` command before marking it `[x]` |\n| TASK-OUTPUT | Default text and JSON output stay byte-identical; quiet adds a branch, never edits an existing line |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n\n`[T###] [DONE | IN PROGRESS | BLOCKED] - one line of evidence`\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\n1. Mark the task `[B]` with the blocking fact\n2. Record the fact beside the task line in `tasks.md`\n3. Continue with the next unblocked task; escalate after two blocked tasks\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ai-execution -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":30,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/217-weak-model-spec-authoring/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/217-weak-model-spec-authoring/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
