 one check per document pair that must agree, or delete the section when the packet holds no paired documents. GOOD: CHK-140 [P1] `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the three phases. WEAK: Docs are verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n<!-- FILL: Name the real approver for each role. Delete a row when the role does not exist. Write `N/A` or delete the section when no sign-off applies. GOOD: Conductor, runs every task. Operator, merges the commit. WEAK: Signed off. -->\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Shell variables used below**: `S` = `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`; `P` = `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the parser loop, `output_text`, and the output dispatch in `recommend-level.sh` (globals near line 122, parser near line 656, dispatch near line 770). Verify: `rg -n 'JSON_OUTPUT|output_text|output_json' $S` prints the global, the two functions, and the dispatch.\n- [ ] T002 [P] Capture baseline outputs into the packet scratch dir. Verify: `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 > $P/scratch/baseline-text.txt && bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 --json > $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt && wc -l < $P/scratch/baseline-text.txt` prints `16`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T003 Add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` to the globals block and a `--quiet|-q` case that sets it to `true` in the parser loop (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n $S` exits 0 and `bash $S --quiet --loc 50 --files 2` exits 0 (no `Unknown option` error).\n- [ ] T004 Add the quiet branch at the top of the output dispatch so `QUIET_OUTPUT=true` prints `Recommended Level: ${RECOMMENDED_LEVEL} (${LEVEL_NAME})` and skips the text/JSON selection (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints exactly `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)` on one line.\n- [ ] T005 [P] Document `--quiet, -q` in `show_help` OPTIONS with one usage example (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -c 'quiet'` prints `2` or more.\n- [ ] T006 [P] Document `--quiet, -q` in the header comment OPTIONS list (`$S`). Verify: `sed -n '13,35p' $S | rg -c 'quiet'` prints `1` or more.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T007 Diff default text output against baseline. Verify: `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 | diff - $P/scratch/baseline-text.txt` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T008 Diff default JSON output against baseline. Verify: `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 --json | diff - $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T009 Pin the quiet line format. Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 | rg -c '^Recommended Level: [0-3] \\((Quick|Baseline|Verification|Full)\\)$'` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T010 Verify quiet wins over `--json`. Verify: `bash $S --quiet --json --loc 500 --files 15 | wc -l` prints `1` and the line does not start with `{`.\n- [ ] T011 Verify the `-q` alias and the error paths. Verify: `bash $S -q --loc 50 --files 2` prints `Recommended Level: 0 (Quick)`; `bash $S --quiet` exits 1 with `ERROR:` on stderr.\n- [ ] T012 Run the existing test scripts that consume `--json`. Verify: `cd .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli && node tests/test-phase-system.js && node tests/test-phase-validation.js` both exit 0.\n- [ ] T013 Run strict packet validation. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $P --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed — `--quiet` prints one line and both default diffs are empty\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Acceptance Criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nRule this packet uses for a blocked task: P0 blocks close; a P1 deferral needs a recorded reason in this file.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented: `rg -c 'REQ-0' $P/spec.md` prints `6` or more\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in `plan.md` §1 and §3\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified — bash only, no new package\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n $S` exits 0\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No stderr noise on success: `bash $S --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 2>$P/scratch/stderr.txt; wc -c < $P/scratch/stderr.txt` prints `0`\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling unchanged: `bash $S --quiet` exits 1 and writes `ERROR:` to stderr\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Follows script patterns: uppercase global, `case` arm, same `echo` label as `output_text`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] Every row of `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met` with observed evidence\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Both baseline diffs (T007, T008) print nothing\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] `-q` alias and `--quiet --json` verified (T010, T011)\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Missing-input error path verified (T011)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\nN/A — this is a feature addition, not a fix packet; there are no actionable findings to classify or inventory.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets — `rg -n 'key|token|secret' $S` shows none\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation unchanged — `--quiet` takes no value, so no new input surface\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] N/A — the script has no auth/authz surface\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] spec/plan/tasks agree on the `--quiet|-q` spelling and the quiet-wins rule\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Header comment and `show_help` document the flag (T005, T006)\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] `runtime/cli/spec/README.md` one-liner stays accurate — no edit needed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Baseline and stderr captures live under `$P/scratch/` only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/`